            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:18",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And David went up at the saying of Gad, which he spake in the name of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:19",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ornan turned back, and saw the angel; and his four sons with him hid themselves. Now Ornan was threshing wheat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:20",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And as David came to Ornan, Ornan looked and saw David, and went out of the threshingfloor, and bowed himself to David with his face to the ground.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 127
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:21",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Then David said to Ornan, Grant me the place of this threshingfloor, that I may build an altar therein unto the Lord: thou shalt grant it me for the full price: that the plague may be stayed from the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:22",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ornan said unto David, Take it to thee, and let my lord the king do that which is good in his eyes: lo, I give thee the oxen also for burnt offerings, and the threshing instruments for wood, and the wheat for the meat offering; I give it all.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 85
          },
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 119
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 133
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:23",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And king David said to Ornan, Nay; but I will verily buy it for the full price: for I will not take that which is thine for the Lord, nor offer burnt offerings without cost.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 104
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 113
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 21:24",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
